The two operations requests are not in this code. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, and that grant is its entire authority. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need filesystem access. Fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need `http-client`. The node holds neither, and there is no WASI adapter. The second request would also send untrusted feed text to an outside service. Adding either one would change the node's declared capabilities in the graph, not just its body. If operations needs these, they should go in a separate node or the host runtime, with their own capability grants (for example an `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` handle).

